{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1402401-m20-great-works","id":1402401,"title":"M20 Great Works","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-12T06:26:24-07:00","id":1402401,"title":"M20 Great Works","content":"Hallo, I'm new to this forum and to M20.<br /> Sorry if there are mistakes in my English, it's not my native language. But I hope you'llget the intent of what I write.<br /> <br /> We started a M20 game not long ago, and now I've been confused about the rules for Great Works.<br /> As far as I understand it, you are allowed to make one Arete roll every 5 hours. But you have to do Stamina rolls to keep going. For an average mage with stamina 2 (or even 3), that would mean he has to roll stamina way before he does the first roll on Arete, right? And since the stamina rolls get harder each time, you're quite fast at a point where you can't make it anymore at all. Or is the rule about stamina rolls only for rituals? <br /> For some effects with Entropy or Mind you might need a lot of successes, e.g. when a Virtual Adept wants to influence some people using a tweet, so it can get into the range of Great Works pretty easily (when I understand correctly that it's a Great work as soon as you need 10 or more successes). The effect itself doesn't have to be very powerful, more like perhaps pushing the people a little bit to liking his tweets or something like that.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I didn't understand those rules correct, but many things seem to be completely unachievable using those rules. I'm happy about every help to sort this out some more. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T06:49:38-07:00","id":1402404,"title":"","content":"Great Works are something that you can take breaks from. As such, I'd exempt them from the Stamina rules. But instead, I'd recommend implementing some sort of milestone system, where there are story goals that must be achieved periodically before you can progress further on the Great Work. This serves the dual purpose of keeping the Great Work from just being a series of rolls and providing an alternate capping mechanism to limit how many rolls you can make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T07:38:18-07:00","id":1402408,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your fast reply!<br /> If I want to implement something like that, it could be in the game like that:<br /> That's a nice idea. That would mean e.g. that the Virtual Adept should e.g. do research on the group of people he wants to effect, then he has to write a nice message as a second step. Then he should do some editing or so. And each of these steps would be one step in the great work? For really big things having more steps?<br /> <br /> I've seen that you can take a break for a maximum of two days, but with technological inventions or computer programming, or if you use this milestone system, would you allow longer pauses from the work between the steps, so you could do the work in the downtime between stories? Would you make a difference depending on the used Focus? (Like a Hermetic Rite not being able to be pasued for long while an Etherite could do so?) Or do you think that would unbalance the game?<br /> <br /> The cap is normally Arete and Willpower added together?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T08:05:02-07:00","id":1402412,"title":"","content":"Double post. See below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 07-12-2020, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T08:07:14-07:00","id":1402413,"title":"","content":"From my understanding, after the first hour of casting you need to roll stamina at difficulty equal to the difficulty of the casting to work an additional hour, and then +1 difficulty thereafter. So, a sphere 3 vulgar work will have difficulty 7 on the stamina roll, meaning making more than 2 rolls is quite hard. But, when you fail a roll, you can spend willpower to continue. This means that you'll generally eat through your Willpower to get more than a few rolls. But... you can also spend willpower to take a break from the work for up to 48 hours, resetting the whole stamina thing, though an esoterica (occult) + wits roll might be needed to pick up where you left off. <br /> <br /> So, let's say you are performing a spell. You could probably spend 5 willpower to get 25 hours (5 rolls) of work, and rest for 2 days and then get maybe 3 more rolls by spending 2 more willpower. <br /> <br /> And this without trying to succeed at any of the stamina rolls. <br /> <br /> Now using life or entropy or something to succeed at those stamina rolls, more rolls might be achieved","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T20:06:43-07:00","id":1402517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1402401-m20-great-works?p=1402408#post1402408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your fast reply!<br /> If I want to implement something like that, it could be in the game like that:<br /> That's a nice idea. That would mean e.g. that the Virtual Adept should e.g. do research on the group of people he wants to effect, then he has to write a nice message as a second step. Then he should do some editing or so. And each of these steps would be one step in the great work? For really big things having more steps?<br /> <br /> I've seen that you can take a break for a maximum of two days, but with technological inventions or computer programming, or if you use this milestone system, would you allow longer pauses from the work between the steps, so you could do the work in the downtime between stories? Would you make a difference depending on the used Focus? (Like a Hermetic Rite not being able to be pasued for long while an Etherite could do so?) Or do you think that would unbalance the game?<br /> <br /> The cap is normally Arete and Willpower added together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that we're firmly in the realm of house rules now, and I'm still working on the specifics of how I'd do this. But the basics would be something along the lines of: there's a limit to the number of rolls you can make between milestones (I'd probably base that on Arete) at which point the casting goes dormant until you achieve your next milestone and you can keep going. Breaks would no longer be limited to two days, and the overall length of the Great Work could in theory extend over weeks, months, years, or even longer, often with long stretches of time passing by with the Great Work being dormant while the mage works to achieve the next milestone. If he never does, then the Great Work remains dormant until he finally gives up on it \u2014 which isn't a function of Willpower so much as of the narrative. <br /> <br /> The nature of the milestones would reflect the Focus used; but the number of them wouldn't, nor would the length of time that the Great Work could go dormant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T15:42:46-07:00","id":1403897,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers and explaining it for me.<br /> I'm sorry I'm late to react, but work caught up on me.<br /> <br /> I think making a house rule for this might be a good idea.<br /> You ideas are greatly appreciated, Dataweaver. Thank you for sharing them.<br /> I especially like the milestone concept. <br /> <br /> I'll discuss the issue with my group. If you're interested in our solution for this, let me know.<br /> <br /> How would you handle magic that builds up an effect over time, like a growing effect? <br /> Would that be a case of a Great work, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}